- `search.query` (input) + `search.clear`, all pointing `data-semtag-controls` at the `entries.view` region wrapping whichever view is active
- Status bar observables: `statusbar.count` (`entries.count`), `statusbar.sort` (`entries.sort`)

**Table view** — collection `entries.table`; rows keyed by database entry id: item anchor on the first field cell (`entries.table.item.entry-1`), per-cell observables `…​.<fieldId>` with state `entry.<fieldId>`, controls `.edit`, `.delete`, `.drag`; sortable column headers `entries.table.header.<fieldId>`; `entries.table.empty` observable.

**Card view** — collection `entries.cards`, item anchor on the card title, same per-field observables and `.edit`/`.delete`/`.drag` controls. Table and card views never render together, so their id namespaces cannot collide at runtime.

**Entry dialog** — region `entry.dialog`, collection `entry.dialog.fields` with one input/toggle per field (`entry.dialog.fields.item.<fieldId>`), sharing state key `entry.<fieldId>` with the display cells so edits and reads connect; `entry.dialog.save` / `entry.dialog.cancel`.

**Field config dialog** — region `fields.dialog`, collection `fields.dialog.list` (name input as item anchor, `.type` select with shared `fieldTypeOptions` string, `.type.option.<type>` items, `.delete`), and the new-field row (`fields.dialog.new.name/.type/.add`).

**404 page** — `notfound.home` navigation → `home.page`.

## Id namespaces
`toolbar.*`, `search.*`, `entries.*` (view region, table/cards collections, empty states), `statusbar.*`, `entry.dialog.*`, `fields.dialog.*`, `notfound.*`. Item keys use runtime database ids (`entry-<ts>-<rand>`, `field-…`) — stable and unique, never array indexes.

